WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:06.030
Welcome to the Microsoft for Education Daily, Tuesday edition.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:09.920
Here's what shipped at Microsoft in the last 24 hours.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:15.960
Safe to learn.

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:20.990
Microsoft's AI privacy standard is now open to every US school district.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:27.500
That's 10 enforceable protections, starting with no AI training on student data.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:36.550
Soon, school IT can lock students' Copilot Chat to Study and Learn,

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:38.090
Microsoft's AI tutor.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:43.870
They can't switch back or use other agents, but can still add their own files.

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:50.140
It's a tutor built to keep the productive struggle, not do students' work.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:55.960
Microsoft's showing schools how to switch it on,

00:00:55.960 --> 00:00:58.150
in webinars on November 10 and 12.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.030
In BC, Alberta or Manitoba? Clocks didn't fall back,

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:07.200
so switch Outlook to your new time zone.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.080
Then recheck meetings after November 1,

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:13.850
especially recurring ones; only organisers can fix them.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:19.970
On managed PCs, Edge will soon let people choose whether it opens at startup.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:25.990
If a student laptop couldn't switch on Smart App Control,

00:01:25.990 --> 00:01:28.070
updates from October 28 fix that.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.840
Building data skills? Microsoft Fabric's Data Days runs to December 15,

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:37.360
with live sessions and study groups.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:42.250
Eligible participants can also find free exam offers for three certifications,

00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:43.290
while they last.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:47.140
The fine print? After November 3,

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:51.410
Entra dynamic groups built on the memberOf preview stop updating.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:53.860
And from December 2,

00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:58.470
GitHub blocks one risky Actions trigger in public repos by default.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:06.860
After hours? GitHub's Game Off jam is on, and this year's theme is Shift.

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:13.540
Go solo or team up, use any engine, and submit your game by December 1.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:18.300
And World of Warcraft: Forever arrives November 4,

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:20.540
with controller support in alpha.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:25.950
Protected data, a tutor that keeps students thinking,

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:29.270
safer code: that's how school stays safe to learn.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.820
Every day, the changelog gets a little longer.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.690
On the release board: shipped, and still shipping.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.410
That was 24 hours at Microsoft. Tomorrow, there's more.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.950
That's the Microsoft for Education Daily for today.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.310
Stay curious. See you tomorrow.
